  "caption": "Quinn discovered bouldering and was a self-declared legend by session three. By week two, the fingers felt like overcooked noodles and the shoulder had joined in.\n\nClimbing injuries tend to gather in the finger pulleys, shoulders and elbows, because fingers adapt more slowly than skill improves. Feeling fine the next morning doesn't always mean fully recovered.\n\nWhat can help: progress grades slowly and favour open-hand grips, warm up the fingers for 10–15 minutes, limit max attempts late in a session, train pushing and shoulder control, and take rest days between hard sessions.\n\nGet it checked if you feel a pop or sharp pain while crimping, finger pain keeps showing up when gripping, or your shoulder aches at night.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
